<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lu'ash</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 738 BCE (approx.) · capital Hatarikka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lu'ash, an Iron Age kingdom of inner Syria centred on Hatarikka, united with Hamath under King Zakkur.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lu'ash occupied the land between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hamath">Hamath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nuhashshe">Nuhashshe</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>. Its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-afis">Hatarikka</a>, the biblical Hadrach, is identified with Tell Afis. It emerged as an Aramaean kingdom in the 9th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Around 800 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakkur">Zakkur</a>, king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hamath">Hamath and Lu'ash</a>, was besieged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-afis">Hatarikka</a> by a coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ben-hadad-iii">Bar-Hadad</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aram-damascus">Aram-Damascus</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> stele, found at Tell Afis, thanks the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalshamin">Baalshamin</a> for deliverance. The kingdom lived from grain farming and the routes of inner <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tiglath-Pileser III of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> annexed Lu'ash in 738 BCE, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-afis">Hatarikka</a> the capital of a province.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 900 BCE – 738 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:3.22%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 738 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hatarikka</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zakkur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Aramaean religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nuhashshe (Iron Age), Hatarikka</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-819&amp;focus=luash" aria-label="Lu'ash on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5639 909 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lu'ash lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5931 1162h0M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5959 1165h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5959 1165h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Syria. <a href="/atlas?year=-819&amp;focus=luash">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

